[Music]  chernobyl is synonymous with danger  driving into the north ukrainian city  we're warned to keep our windows shut  radiation levels in some spots remain  dangerously high 36 years since the  world's worst nuclear plant disaster  engineer alexander skereta and his  colleagues are responsible for  maintaining the area around the  notorious nuclear plant they're only  permitted to live here 15 days per month  to limit their exposure which makes the  russian military's actions here  difficult to comprehend  the whole world knows about chernobyl he  says  i can't understand the russian brain  what were they thinking after the  russian retreat skereta returned to work  to find this his office like so many  others here ransacked and looted his  computer among the thousands of pieces  of highly sensitive and expensive  equipment either stolen or destroyed  they made a mess of everything he says  chernobyl sits a short drive from the  belarus border and was quickly captured  by russian troops on the first day of  the invasion  this resident says the russians caught  her trying to contact ukrainian  authorities  they forced me to my knees with a gun to  my head she says i thought i was going  to die when the russians finally left  after five weeks she says they strapped  washing machines and other household  appliances to the tops of their tanks  but the greatest damage done by russian  soldiers here might have actually been  to themselves this is the edge of the  so-called red forest in chernobyl and it  has that name because a lot of evergreen  trees here have turned a shade of  reddish orange as a result of the high  level of radiation that exists on the  soil we're only being allowed to visit  here for a few minutes but it seems the  russians stayed here for a few weeks not  only in the red forest but digging  trenches in the soil there are food  containers scattered all around here  they even used some of the sand  to make sandbags  you have to be crazy or stupid to do  that kind of thing do they have a death  wish ask this member of ukraine's  national guard he showed us numerous  examples where the russians trampled  bulldozed and dug up one of the most  toxic places on earth possibly inhaling  the dangerous dust  our informants in belarus told us that  some of the russian soldiers who stayed  in those trenches were later  hospitalized he says ukraine's nuclear  scientists say radiation levels at the  chernobyl site are now safe but the  russian activity disrupted enough soil  to create additional radiation hot spots  the worst case scenario once feared was  avoided but more than two months since  russian troops left this area crews have  barely begun to clean up their mess jeff  semple global news chernobyl

